# Legacy Cursor compatibility rule

Read and follow `AGENTS.md` at the repository root before changing files. It is
the authoritative source for SBK architecture, safety constraints, coding
conventions, task-specific reading, and verification. Inspect the working tree
first and preserve unrelated changes. Use the relevant guide under `docs/` and
the nearest component or driver README; do not copy rules into this legacy
file.

Before editing a writer, reader, driver operation, PerL queue/recorder, or SBM
measurement path, read `docs/HOT_PATHS.md` and obtain the specific explicit
approval required there before adding any per-operation or per-measurement
work.
